From: Yocto build fix
Subject: [PATCH] CMakeLists: preserve toolchain-provided CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS

Upstream CMakeLists.txt rebuilds CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS from
CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_INIT (which is only seeded from the CXXFLAGS
environment variable), discarding the architecture flags
(-mthumb -mfpu=neon -mfloat-abi=hard -mcpu=... etc.) that OE's
generated toolchain.cmake sets on CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS itself. Without
those flags the cross compiler falls back to its default (soft-float)
target, which then fails to include <gnu/stubs-soft.h> against a
sysroot whose glibc was built hard-float only.

Preserve whatever CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS the toolchain file already set
instead of discarding it.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe-specific cross-compile toolchain fix]

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@
 
 SET(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 14)
 set(CMAKE_MODULE_PATH ${CMAKE_MODULE_PATH} "${PROJECT_SOURCE_DIR}/cmake_modules/")
-set(CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS "${CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_INIT} -fPIC -Wall -pedantic")
+set(CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS "${CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS} -fPIC -Wall -pedantic")
 set(CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_DEBUG "-g -O0")
 set(CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_RELEASE "-g -O3")
